# Tell Docker what to exclude from the build context. Without this file, Docker
# copies your entire project directory into the image including .venv (hundreds of MB), .env (contains secrets),
# *.db (runtime data), and .git (version history). The image becomes bloated and potentially leaks credentials.
#
# .dockerignore works exactly like .gitignore — same syntax, same idea.
#
#
.venv/
.env
*.db
*.db-shm
*.db-wal
.git/
__pycache__/
*.pyc
.pytest_cache/
.idea/
.remember/
tests/
README.md